WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.270
In this lesson, you will learn to Snap
windows with the keyboard.

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:09.147
When you are typing, reaching for the
mouse breaks your flow.

00:00:09.147 --> 00:00:10.073
With a shortcut,

00:00:10.073 --> 00:00:13.947
a window goes to its place in the time it
takes to press four keys.

00:00:15.313 --> 00:00:19.242
The shortcuts act on the focused window:
the one you are typing in.

00:00:19.242 --> 00:00:20.884
This Layout has three Zones.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:26.051
Press Control, Option, Shift, and the
number two. The window goes to Zone 2.

00:00:26.464 --> 00:00:31.413
Control, Option, Shift and one send it to
Zone 1. Any Zone, one shortcut.

00:00:31.977 --> 00:00:34.398
The square brackets step through the
Zones.

00:00:34.398 --> 00:00:38.789
Control, Option, Shift and the right
bracket move the window to the next Zone.

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:42.312
The left bracket moves it back to the
previous one.

00:00:42.312 --> 00:00:45.168
From the last Zone, the next one is the
first again.

00:00:45.881 --> 00:00:48.883
Zones are numbered top to bottom, then
left to right.

00:00:48.883 --> 00:00:51.659
They are the same numbers you see in the
overlay.

00:00:52.029 --> 00:00:56.120
So a glance at the overlay while you drag
teaches you the shortcuts.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:59.610
Your main work is always Zone 2, your
notes always Zone 3.

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:06.194
To change a shortcut, open Settings from
the menu-bar menu, then the Hotkeys tab.

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:10.954
Click a shortcut, and press the new
combination. It works at once.

00:01:10.954 --> 00:01:13.477
Every shortcut needs Control or Command.

00:01:15.101 --> 00:01:17.672
Here is how people use the shortcuts every
day.

00:01:18.022 --> 00:01:21.757
Keep your main work in the same Zone, for
example Zone 2.

00:01:21.757 --> 00:01:26.410
Then Control, Option, Shift and 2 becomes
your reflex for back to work.

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:30.942
You just opened a new window? Send it to
its Zone without leaving the keyboard.

00:01:31.292 --> 00:01:32.546
And Control, Option,

00:01:32.546 --> 00:01:36.621
Shift and the backtick key switch the
display to its next Layout,

00:01:36.621 --> 00:01:39.692
for example from focused work to a meeting
setup.

00:01:41.242 --> 00:01:41.824
To recap.

00:01:41.824 --> 00:01:46.544
Control, Option, Shift and a number Snap
the focused window to that Zone.

00:01:46.544 --> 00:01:50.230
The square brackets move it to the
previous or next Zone.

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:53.786
And you can change every shortcut in
Settings, Hotkeys.

00:01:55.336 --> 00:02:00.087
In the next lesson, you will learn to
resize two windows that sit side by side,

00:02:00.087 --> 00:02:01.590
together, in one gesture.
